==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Thundia, type β''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Divine Thundia β''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

Evolves into '''Ultimate Thundia β''' at level 60 using [[Catfruit]], [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
This unit is very similar to [[Windy (Uber Rare Cat)|Windy]], except Thundia deals [[Massive Damage]] to [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] instead of [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemies. Thundia is a simple unit, she stays in the back and, if well protected, she will sometimes land a powerful attack that will heavily cripple any Red enemy caught in the blast, all while dealing acceptable damage to other enemies. If this sounds familiar, it's due to this unit's many similarities to [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]], who works the same way.

It is very important to properly defend her by using either cheap meatshields or the many units who specialize in blocking the advance of Red enemies, such as [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fried Shrimp Cat]], [[Bondage Cat (Special Cat)|Bondage Cat]] (if [[Talents|talented]]), [[Viking Cat (Rare Cat)|Viking Cat]] or even [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]], all while possibly avoiding units who can knockback Red (e.g. [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Pirate Cat]]), as those cats make a terrible synergy with Thundia.

Despite the potential to deal a lot of damage, Thundia has a very inconveniently long attack rate, causing missed hits to become increasingly problematic as enemies begin pushing into your backlines. Luckily, Red enemies often struggle to take advantage of this, making Thundia a good match for them.

Notably, Thundia can pose a viable threat to [[Capy]], [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] and [[J.K. Bun Bun]]. Unfortunately, high range enemies (or those with a manner of pierce) can severely hinder her performance; examples are [[Two Can]], [[Professor A.]], and [[Hackey]], which either repeatedly juggle her to death, or can strike her through a large effective range.

==='''True Form'''===
Divine Thundia β finally receives the stats she needs to keep up with stronger enemies. She gains buffs in health, attack, range, and speed, all of which are massive boosts and really helps her stay relevant in the midgame. Her health gets doubled, giving her much better survivability. She also gets an attack buff, making her DPS decent for her range, which also increases to 440, making it easier for her to deal with backliners, like [[Le'noir]]. Lastly, she gets double her original speed, making her a lot less sluggish when reaching the frontlines. Thus, overall, if you did not have a good reason to bring her into battle already, then you most certainly have one now.

==='''Ultra Form'''===
Thundia's Ultra Form, Ultimate Thundia β, brings a set of improvements that drastically change her utility. First and foremost, she has gained a [[Multi-Hit|Multi‑Hit]] [[Long Distance]] attack that pierces up to 920 range, letting her hit even Professor A. with stepping stones. The only caveat is the fact that the attacks only overlap at her standing range—which hardly matters since the first attack is more than likely going to stagger enemies, allowing them to be struck by the subsequent attack. The Multi‑Hit effectively increases her DPS by a whopping 40% on average despite her attack rate increase. This damage is absurdly high, and makes her one of the most proficient anti‑Red nuker in the game, especially when Talents are involved.

Her survivability has also been massively upscaled, which is complemented by the [[Survive]] ability. The range increase doesn't change any notable matchups, but it generally allows her to strike enemies from a safer distance; Ultimate Thundia β's HP makes it nearly impossible for enemies to take her down before she gets at least a few attacks off. Along with [[Immune to Slow|her]] [[Immune to Weaken|immunities]], these can be seen as quality‑of‑life benefits, since her survivability was never an issue even at Divine Thundia β's range. With this, now you're fully capable of getting even a second Ultimate Thundia β out on the field, and even a third!

The most questionable aspect of this Ultra Form is the necessity of such a role, since there are seldom use cases where such overkill is needed. Red is one of the most manageable traits in the game, meaning Ultimate Thundia β's most potent advantages are her performance as a generalist as well as a specialist. In this department, Thundia has the stats necessary to rival and surpass Ultimate Windy α as a generalist/specialist nuker.

Regardless, if you're not in need of such powerful anti‑Red firepower, the benefits this Ultra Form brings shouldn't be considered as heavily. While Ultimate Thundia β is undoubtedly the best in her niche and a fantastic generalist overall, that niche is trivial at the stage of the game you unlock this form in. The [[Catseye|Dark Catseyes]] required to unlock it can be unnecessary if one is already satisfied with Divine Thundia β's/any other anti-Red's performance.

==='''Talents'''===
'''[[Special Abilities#Resist|Wave Resist]]''' can theoretically be turned into complete [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]] with a Resist Wave [[Talent Orbs|Talent Orb]]. Despite this, Massive Damage Up Orbs are typically what you'll use her with, unless running it up with [[Berserkory]] or Two Can. As such, this Talent should be avoided unless under those niche circumstances.

'''[[Immune to Curse|Curse Immunity]]''' is also avoidable, as Thundia is hardly used in Relic centric stages against enemies she doesn't already outrange.

'''Attack Buff''' and '''[[Strengthen]]''' are what you should focus on most, with '''Defense Buff''' being great at giving her more opportunities to reposition if you have the NP to spare. This is especially true if you plan on unlocking her Ultra Form, which synergizes intensely with these Talents. To put her damage into perspective with full investment: at Lv.60 in Ultra Form, she can deal up to an astounding '''''1.4 million damage''''' to Red enemies per attack cycle if Strengthened. Should you be willing to invest in her, both in levels and NP, you can turn Thundia into your most powerful Red killer!

{{Job|Classification = Nuker & Backliner|UltraClass = Nuker & Sniper}}

