==Trivia==
*She was added alongside [[Windy (Uber Rare Cat)|Windy]] on December 25th, 2013.
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Thundia, type β was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Thunder and Lightning (Removed Combo)|Thunder and Lightning]] and [[Curves (Removed Combo)|Curves]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.3 Update|Version 15.3]], Thundia's English True and Ultra Forms' names lacked the "β" part.
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Thundia's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Thundia
A galaxy girl who can manipulate electricity.
Brings down bolts from a distance.
Massive damage to Red enemies. (Area Attack)</pre>
<pre>Thundia, type β
Always worries about her chronic neck pain.
Likes watching cartoons in her spare time.
Massive damage to Red enemies. (Area Attack)</pre>
<pre>Divine Thundia β
When you have a goddess' body, it's tough to find
clothes that fit. Long distance Area Attacks
deliver massive damage to Red enemies.</pre>
<pre>Ultimate Thundia β
Her popularity skyrocketed after a combat glow-up.
Calls down long-range Area thunder attacks that
deal Massive damage to Red enemies.</pre>
*Similarly to [[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Kai]] and Windy, Thundia also doubles in base health and speed when gaining her True Form. She also has the same stats as Windy, with the exception of different trait targeting, 10 less range and 1 less knockback.
*The outlets on Divine Thundia β and Ultimate Thundia β's "tails" match up perfectly with the plugs on Divine Windy α and Ultimate Windy α's tails respectively.
*Thundia takes after [[wikipedia:Raijin|Raijin]] for her theme. Circular drums are a common trait found in depictions of Raijin. Raijin is also commonly portrayed as a pair with [[wikipedia:Fūjin|Fujin]], which is what Windy is themed after.
*In the [[Media:Galaxygals img01-03.png|first version]] of the Galaxy Gals' event poster, Thundia is said to enjoy games in addition to cartoons. This information was omitted from later versions for unknown reasons.
*In [[The Battle Cats POP!]], Thundia's description mispells "Brings" as "Briings".

